  "implementation_scope": {
    "PHX-121": "Scoped generic forward prototype only. Retain all x86 compat declarations: their deletion without matching conversions is unsafe and deliberately excluded, not silently applied.",
    "PHX-124": "Adapt local f_delown __f_setown name; map all TID/TGID/PGRP producers/decoders coherently. Add NULL guards around BOTH RCU pid_task results before SIGIO and SIGURG dispatch. Preserve group tasklist iteration, owner lock, permission hooks and SIGURG return contract.",
    "PHX-125": "After corrected124, enum owner type reaches both helpers; retain current int/group do_send_sig_info boundary via type!=PIDTYPE_PID. Typed signal chain126-137 is NOT applied in this phase.",
    "PHX-142": "Replace wrong donor arithmetic and old255 sentinel with dedicated atomic pipe report containing all six child-only counter deltas. Preserve parent failures, require exact test count, validate underflow/overflow, reject short/absent reports without blocking after wait, reject abnormal exits. No counts in8-bit exit status.",
    "PHX-143": "Two nested PID43 allocation/reuse tests after invalid ancestor PID, on corrected142 interface. Six nested cases; total plan29. PID_NS config remains disabled for miatoll.",
    "PHX-144": "Real native32-bit ARM copy_thread_tls conversion. CLONE_SETTLS consumes explicit tls; existing register/frame/kernel-thread handling preserved. Not an ARM64 compat backend replacement.",
    "PHX-145": "Add clone3 missing-TLS compile guard only after auditing all four explicitly clone3-capable architectures. Real Xtensa copy_thread_tls prerequisite adapted from upstream c346b94f8c5d1b7d637522c908209de93305a8eb, including explicit tls rather than areg[5]. ARM64/x86 backends already implemented. No fake HAVE_COPY_THREAD_TLS selection.",
    "PHX-149": "Actual Android donor behavior: unconditional FunctionFS special/genfs classification, no new policycap enum/array ABI entry. No userspace policy edits/blanket allow. Enforcing ROM USB/ADB and multiple-mount label tests remain mandatory.",
    "PHX-150": "Add securityfs to existing SE_SBGENFS mount set. It is not special in-core setxattr handling and does NOT add chcon support. Per-file enforcing policy validation remains outstanding."
  },
